# play main-menu/00-tui-main -----------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the gallery's$
# fixture plans. Nothing on this machine changes: the simulated$
# system only records each step it would apply, and the record$
# is shown when play ends.$
$
hardn  v0.4.0              https://github.com/abbott/hardn$
$
# Debian 12 (Bookworm) #########################################$
$
  [BOS-SAN-L01]            192.0.2.10$
                           182 days, 2 hours, 26 minutes$
$
  [*] Risk Level           Moderate ~ medium security$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
  [+] Firewall             Configured deny policy$
  [+] SSH Login            Configured root disallowed$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured key-only auth$
  [+] SSH Port             Configured non-default (2230)$
  [ ] AppArmor             Not Configured$
  [ ] Auto Updates         Not Configured$
$
----------------------------------------------------------------$
$
  Select an option         Mode Live$
$
   1) User Management      Create, Configure (sudo, SSH keys)$
   2) SSH Login            Root login, passwords, port$
   3) DNS                  Configure Nameservers$
   4) Firewall             Configure UFW rules$
   5) Backup               Configure Hardn backup settings$
   6) Auto Updates         Configure automatic updates$
   7) Run All              Execute hardening operations$
   8) Environment          Keep HARDN_CONFIG$
   9) System Details       View system information$
  10) Logs                 View log file$
$
   0) Exit                 q to quit$
$
  > Enter selection [0-10 or q]: 3$
$
# Info: dns/debian13$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13; /etc/resolv.conf is a file$
# dhcpcd wrote from eth0's lease, naming 192.0.2.1 and$
# example.net. hardn.yml lists 192.0.2.54, 2001:db8::54. Each$
# item is a change on the real engine, confirmed y/N; then the$
# screen is read again.$
$
# DNS Configuration ############################################$
$
# Current DNS Configuration ------------------------------------$
$
   -  DNS Implementation   direct (/etc/resolv.conf)$
   -  Nameservers          192.0.2.1$
   -  Search Domains       example.net$
$
# Configured Nameservers ---------------------------------------$
$
   -  Nameserver 1         192.0.2.54$
   -  Nameserver 2         2001:db8::54$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Configure DNS        Apply nameserver settings from con...$
   2) Add nameserver       Add a new DNS server to configuration$
   3) Remove nameserver    Remove a DNS server from configura...$
   4) Use Cloudflare DNS   Set nameservers to 1.1.1.1, 1.0.0.1$
   5) Use Google DNS       Set nameservers to 8.8.8.8, 8.8.4.4$
   6) Use Quad9 DNS        Set nameservers to 9.9.9.9, 149.11...$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-6 or q]: 2$
$
# Add nameserver ###############################################$
$
  Enter nameserver IP address [0 or q]: 999.1.1.1$
  (x) Invalid IP address format$
  Enter nameserver IP address [0 or q]: 192.0.2.54$
  (x) Nameserver 192.0.2.54 is already configured$
  Enter nameserver IP address [0 or q]: 192.0.2.53$
$
# DNS Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Nameservers          192.0.2.54, 2001:db8::54, 192.0.2.53$
   -  Search Domains       example.net$
  [ ] dhcpcd may rewrite /etc/resolv.conf on a lease$
$
   -  Set the nameservers$
      /etc/resolv.conf$
      @@ -1,3 +1,5 @@$
       # Generated by dhcpcd from eth0.dhcp$
       search example.net$
      -nameserver 192.0.2.1$
      +nameserver 192.0.2.54$
      +nameserver 2001:db8::54$
      +nameserver 192.0.2.53$
$
   -  Save the configuration$
      /etc/hardn/hardn.yml$
      @@ -3,3 +3,4 @@$
       nameservers:$
         - "192.0.2.54"$
         - "2001:db8::54"$
      +  - "192.0.2.53"$
$
  Add nameserver 192.0.2.53? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Set the nameservers     Done$
  [+] Save the configuration  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  Backup of /etc/resolv.conf, /etc/hardn/hardn.yml kept in$
  /var/backups/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
